<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afghan–Sikh Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1748–1837</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Afghan–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> Wars were a series of conflicts between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghans">Afghans</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhs">Sikhs</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, from the invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> in 1748 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jamrud">Battle of Jamrud</a> in 1837. The Sikhs first resisted as independent misls and later, united under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a> (1818), <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> (1819) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshawar">Peshawar</a> (1834) from Afghan control, ending Afghan rule east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khyber-pass">Khyber Pass</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afghan-sikh-wars.jpg" alt="Afghan–Sikh Wars" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Basahatullah (Basharat Ullah), court painter of the Maharaja of Nabha · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afghan-Sikh_Wars_depiction.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
